msgid "Part 4 — Serialisation"
msgstr "Partie 4 — Sérialisation"

msgid ""
"A nested dictionary can be saved to a file and read back, in JSON or with"
" pickle. This part saves the heating schedule of the house, which maps an"
" hour of the day to a temperature, and explains what each format keeps."
msgstr ""
"Un dictionnaire imbriqué peut être enregistré dans un fichier puis relu, "
"en JSON ou avec pickle. Cette partie enregistre la programmation du "
"chauffage de la maison, qui associe une heure de la journée à une "
"température, et explique ce que conserve chaque format."

msgid ""
"The thermostat of each room switches at given hours. The hours are "
"integers, not strings:"
msgstr ""
"Le thermostat de chaque pièce change de consigne à des heures données. "
"Les heures sont des entiers, pas des chaînes :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> schedule = NestedDictionary({\n"
"...     \"living room\": {\"thermostat\": {7: 20.5, 22: 17.0}},\n"
"...     \"bedroom\": {\"thermostat\": {6: 19.0, 21: 16.5}},\n"
"... })"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> schedule = NestedDictionary({\n"
"...     \"living room\": {\"thermostat\": {7: 20.5, 22: 17.0}},\n"
"...     \"bedroom\": {\"thermostat\": {6: 19.0, 21: 16.5}},\n"
"... })"

msgid "JSON"
msgstr "JSON"

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.to_json` writes the dictionary to a "
"JSON file. ``indent`` makes the file easier to read:"
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.to_json` écrit le dictionnaire dans "
"un fichier JSON. ``indent`` rend le fichier plus lisible :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> schedule.to_json(\"schedule.json\", indent=2)\n"
">>> from pathlib import Path\n"
">>> print(Path(\"schedule.json\").read_text())\n"
"{\n"
"  \"living room\": {\n"
"    \"thermostat\": {\n"
"      \"[7]\": 20.5,\n"
"      \"[22]\": 17.0\n"
"    }\n"
"  },\n"
"  \"bedroom\": {\n"
"    \"thermostat\": {\n"
"      \"[6]\": 19.0,\n"
"      \"[21]\": 16.5\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
">>> schedule.to_json(\"schedule.json\", indent=2)\n"
">>> from pathlib import Path\n"
">>> print(Path(\"schedule.json\").read_text())\n"
"{\n"
"  \"living room\": {\n"
"    \"thermostat\": {\n"
"      \"[7]\": 20.5,\n"
"      \"[22]\": 17.0\n"
"    }\n"
"  },\n"
"  \"bedroom\": {\n"
"    \"thermostat\": {\n"
"      \"[6]\": 19.0,\n"
"      \"[21]\": 16.5\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}"

msgid ""
"JSON only allows string keys, so the hours are written as ``\"[7]\"``, "
"``\"[22]\"`` and so on. :meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_json` "
"reads them back as integers:"
msgstr ""
"JSON n’autorise que des clés de type chaîne ; les heures sont donc "
"écrites ``\"[7]\"``, ``\"[22]\"``, et ainsi de suite. "
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_json` les relit comme des "
"entiers :"

msgid ""
">>> restored = NestedDictionary.from_json(\"schedule.json\")\n"
">>> restored[[\"living room\", \"thermostat\", 7]]\n"
"20.5\n"
">>> restored == schedule\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> restored = NestedDictionary.from_json(\"schedule.json\")\n"
">>> restored[[\"living room\", \"thermostat\", 7]]\n"
"20.5\n"
">>> restored == schedule\n"
"True"

msgid ""
"The file holds the content only: neither the class nor the "
"``default_setup``. The result has the class on which ``from_json`` is "
"called and, unless ``default_setup`` is given, the default configuration "
"of that class, as with :meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_dict`. "
"The same file can give a :class:`~ndict_tools.StrictNestedDictionary`, or"
" a dictionary printed with an indentation:"
msgstr ""
"Le fichier ne contient que le contenu : ni la classe ni le "
"``default_setup``. Le résultat a la classe sur laquelle ``from_json`` est"
" appelée et, sauf si ``default_setup`` est fourni, la configuration par "
"défaut de cette classe, comme avec "
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_dict`. Le même fichier peut "
"donner un :class:`~ndict_tools.StrictNestedDictionary`, ou un "
"dictionnaire affiché avec une indentation :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import StrictNestedDictionary\n"
">>> checked = StrictNestedDictionary.from_json(\"schedule.json\")\n"
">>> checked.isomorph(schedule)\n"
"True\n"
">>> printable = NestedDictionary.from_json(\n"
"...     \"schedule.json\",\n"
"...     default_setup={\"indent\": 2, \"default_factory\": "
"NestedDictionary},\n"
"... )\n"
">>> printable.default_setup[0]\n"
"('indent', 2)"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import StrictNestedDictionary\n"
">>> checked = StrictNestedDictionary.from_json(\"schedule.json\")\n"
">>> checked.isomorph(schedule)\n"
"True\n"
">>> printable = NestedDictionary.from_json(\n"
"...     \"schedule.json\",\n"
"...     default_setup={\"indent\": 2, \"default_factory\": "
"NestedDictionary},\n"
"... )\n"
">>> printable.default_setup[0]\n"
"('indent', 2)"

msgid ""
"Keys of type :class:`str`, :class:`int`, :class:`float` and "
":class:`bool`, and tuples and frozensets of such values, survive the "
"round trip. A string key that looks like an encoded key is escaped, so it"
" stays a string:"
msgstr ""
"Les clés de type :class:`str`, :class:`int`, :class:`float` et "
":class:`bool`, ainsi que les tuples et les frozensets de telles valeurs, "
"survivent à l’aller-retour. Une clé chaîne qui ressemble à une clé "
"encodée est échappée, et reste donc une chaîne :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> labels = NestedDictionary({7: \"wake up\", \"[7]\": \"a label\"})\n"
">>> labels.to_json(\"labels.json\")\n"
">>> NestedDictionary.from_json(\"labels.json\").to_dict()\n"
"{7: 'wake up', '[7]': 'a label'}"
msgstr ""
">>> labels = NestedDictionary({7: \"wake up\", \"[7]\": \"a label\"})\n"
">>> labels.to_json(\"labels.json\")\n"
">>> NestedDictionary.from_json(\"labels.json\").to_dict()\n"
"{7: 'wake up', '[7]': 'a label'}"

msgid ""
"A key of another type raises :class:`~ndict_tools.StackedTypeError`. The "
"values must be types that JSON can write: strings, numbers, booleans, "
"``None``, lists and dictionaries."
msgstr ""
"Une clé d’un autre type lève une :class:`~ndict_tools.StackedTypeError`. "
"Les valeurs doivent être de types que JSON sait écrire : chaînes, "
"nombres, booléens, ``None``, listes et dictionnaires."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> NestedDictionary({None: \"unknown hour\"}).to_json(\"unknown.json\")\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"ndict_tools.exception.StackedTypeError: JSON key encoding is not "
"supported for type NoneType. Supported types: str, int, float, bool, "
"tuple, frozenset. (expected: str, got: NoneType)"
msgstr ""
">>> NestedDictionary({None: \"unknown hour\"}).to_json(\"unknown.json\")\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"ndict_tools.exception.StackedTypeError: JSON key encoding is not "
"supported for type NoneType. Supported types: str, int, float, bool, "
"tuple, frozenset. (expected: str, got: NoneType)"

msgid "Pickle"
msgstr "Pickle"

msgid ""
"Loading a pickle file can run arbitrary code. Only load files that you "
"wrote yourself or that come from a source you trust. ``to_pickle`` and "
"``from_pickle`` emit a :class:`UserWarning` as a reminder; the examples "
"below hide it."
msgstr ""
"Charger un fichier pickle peut exécuter du code arbitraire. Ne chargez "
"que des fichiers que vous avez écrits vous-même ou qui proviennent d’une "
"source de confiance. ``to_pickle`` et ``from_pickle`` émettent un "
":class:`UserWarning` pour le rappeler ; les exemples ci-dessous le "
"masquent."

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.to_pickle` writes the whole object, "
"and next to it a ``.sha256`` file that holds the digest of the pickle "
"file:"
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.to_pickle` écrit l’objet entier et, "
"à côté, un fichier ``.sha256`` qui contient l’empreinte du fichier pickle"
" :"

msgid ""
">>> schedule.to_pickle(\"schedule.pkl\")\n"
">>> sorted(path.name for path in Path().glob(\"schedule.pkl*\"))\n"
"['schedule.pkl', 'schedule.pkl.sha256']"
msgstr ""
">>> schedule.to_pickle(\"schedule.pkl\")\n"
">>> sorted(path.name for path in Path().glob(\"schedule.pkl*\"))\n"
"['schedule.pkl', 'schedule.pkl.sha256']"

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_pickle` checks the digest, then"
" returns the object with its class and its ``default_setup``, with no "
"argument to give:"
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_pickle` vérifie l’empreinte, "
"puis renvoie l’objet avec sa classe et son ``default_setup``, sans "
"argument à fournir :"

msgid ""
">>> NestedDictionary.from_pickle(\"schedule.pkl\") == schedule\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> NestedDictionary.from_pickle(\"schedule.pkl\") == schedule\n"
"True"

msgid ""
"If the file was changed after it was written, or if the ``.sha256`` file "
"is missing, ``from_pickle`` raises "
":class:`~ndict_tools.StackedValueError` before loading anything:"
msgstr ""
"Si le fichier a été modifié après son écriture, ou si le fichier "
"``.sha256`` est absent, ``from_pickle`` lève une "
":class:`~ndict_tools.StackedValueError` avant de charger quoi que ce soit"
" :"

msgid ""
">>> with open(\"schedule.pkl\", \"ab\") as file:\n"
"...     _ = file.write(b\"tampered\")\n"
">>> NestedDictionary.from_pickle(\"schedule.pkl\")\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"ndict_tools.exception.StackedValueError: SHA-256 digest mismatch for "
"'schedule.pkl': ..."
msgstr ""
">>> with open(\"schedule.pkl\", \"ab\") as file:\n"
"...     _ = file.write(b\"tampered\")\n"
">>> NestedDictionary.from_pickle(\"schedule.pkl\")\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"ndict_tools.exception.StackedValueError: SHA-256 digest mismatch for "
"'schedule.pkl': ..."

msgid ""
"``verify=False`` skips the check, for a file whose origin you trust and "
"whose digest file was not kept."
msgstr ""
"``verify=False`` ignore la vérification, pour un fichier dont vous "
"connaissez l’origine et dont le fichier d’empreinte n’a pas été conservé."

msgid ""
"The object in the file must be an instance of the class on which "
"``from_pickle`` is called, or of a subclass. Otherwise "
":class:`~ndict_tools.StackedTypeError` is raised:"
msgstr ""
"L’objet contenu dans le fichier doit être une instance de la classe sur "
"laquelle ``from_pickle`` est appelée, ou d’une sous-classe. Sinon, une "
":class:`~ndict_tools.StackedTypeError` est levée :"

msgid ""
">>> schedule.to_pickle(\"schedule.pkl\")\n"
">>> StrictNestedDictionary.from_pickle(\"schedule.pkl\")\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"ndict_tools.exception.StackedTypeError: 'schedule.pkl' does not contain "
"an instance of StrictNestedDictionary (expected: StrictNestedDictionary, "
"got: NestedDictionary)"
msgstr ""
">>> schedule.to_pickle(\"schedule.pkl\")\n"
">>> StrictNestedDictionary.from_pickle(\"schedule.pkl\")\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"ndict_tools.exception.StackedTypeError: 'schedule.pkl' does not contain "
"an instance of StrictNestedDictionary (expected: StrictNestedDictionary, "
"got: NestedDictionary)"

msgid "Choosing a format"
msgstr "Choisir un format"

msgid "Keys"
msgstr "Clés"

msgid "``str``, ``int``, ``float``, ``bool``, and tuples or frozensets of these"
msgstr "``str``, ``int``, ``float``, ``bool``, et tuples ou frozensets de ceux-ci"

msgid "Any hashable value"
msgstr "Toute valeur hachable"

msgid "Values"
msgstr "Valeurs"

msgid "Strings, numbers, booleans, ``None``, lists, dictionaries"
msgstr "Chaînes, nombres, booléens, ``None``, listes, dictionnaires"

msgid "Any value pickle can write"
msgstr "Toute valeur que pickle sait écrire"

msgid "Class and ``default_setup``"
msgstr "Classe et ``default_setup``"

msgid "Chosen when reading"
msgstr "Choisies à la lecture"

msgid "Kept"
msgstr "Conservées"

msgid "Readable by"
msgstr "Lisible par"

msgid "Any language and tool"
msgstr "Tout langage et tout outil"

msgid "Python only"
msgstr "Python uniquement"

msgid "Loading from an untrusted source"
msgstr "Chargement depuis une source non fiable"

msgid "Safe"
msgstr "Sans danger"

msgid "Never"
msgstr "Jamais"

msgid "Integrity check"
msgstr "Contrôle d’intégrité"

msgid "None"
msgstr "Aucun"

msgid "SHA-256 digest file"
msgstr "Fichier d’empreinte SHA-256"

msgid ""
"Use JSON for configuration files, data exchanged with other programs, and"
" anything that comes from outside. Use pickle to keep Python objects "
"between two runs of your own program."
msgstr ""
"Utilisez JSON pour les fichiers de configuration, les données échangées "
"avec d’autres programmes et tout ce qui vient de l’extérieur. Utilisez "
"pickle pour conserver des objets Python entre deux exécutions de votre "
"propre programme."

